{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JcYFb8BBxEqPz19FawZ8vk","type":"tool_result","content":"----\n# WI-841 first-approval adjudication at be1e431\n\nQuestion: is each Drafted row ready to be APPROVED as it stands, or does it go back with findings?\nChains read: SR-154, SR-156, SR-227 (all parents Approved). Rows judged: LLR-307, LLR-308, LLR-309, TC-325, TC-326, TC-327, TC-328.\n\n- [RETURN] LLR-307 -> one digest and covering predicate for a changed Done-when, which owes a blessing only when a readable current checklist differs from a readable claim and has no cover, and owes nothing when the claim or the current checklist is missing -> SR-156 says the blessing binds the changed text before any later build, close or landing, through a seam its parent calls fail-closed (SN-008). `kitlib.done_when.blessing` answers None for an unreadable claim copy, so `lane_hold` holds nothing at dispatch, at a hand close or at the merge ladder, and the merge-time mint, which uses the same `blessing`, mints nothing. Meanwhile `adjudicate_brief._subject_claim` REFUSES to compose the brief for that same unreadable claim -> not ready: the row writes \"missing\" and \"unreadable\" as one case and gives no reason, so an unreadable claim fails OPEN at all three holds and at the safety net. It is the one place where the hold and the brief that should release it disagree. No TC checks the missing-claim or unreadable-claim arm. Also, the row says the digest is \"sha256 truncated to 16 hexadecimal characters\", but the bound token (and the `digest=` a verdict must carry) is `sha256:<16 hex>`. A judge following the text would write a digest that never matches\n- [RETURN] LLR-308 -> (a) a done-when brief class: one work item, claim read at the lane base or the claim commit, refusal on an unreadable claim, missing Context or unchanged checklist, rendered items/changes/digest/clipped Context, DONE-WHEN grammar; AND (b) a combined sitting class: kind tokens, fixed composition order, whole refusal, verdict checked against the requested kinds -> SR-156, its only parent, calls for an in-lane blessing of the changed text, which justifies (a). No SR in the registry calls for combining amendment, first-approval and done-when judgements into one sitting (grep for combined/sitting/checkpoint finds none) -> not ready: two decisions in one row, and the combined half answers a requirement no parent makes (scope, not detail). TC-327 also leaves (a)'s refusals for an unreadable claim and a missing Context, the post-closure claim read and the stated clip unverified. \"changes and digest counters\" calls a digest a counter\n- [APPROVE] LLR-309 -> before a build or rework session `build_hold` returns HELD while LLR-307's `lane_hold` owes a blessing; the merge ladder refuses an unblessed changed closed checklist after its close records; the pre-commit `done-when-blessed` step refuses a staged move out of active with no binding blessing; each arm names digest and changes; review sessions, adjudication rows, the editing commit and test runs are not held -> it covers exactly SR-156's three new hold points and its exemptions, and it matches `docs/decisions/wi-841.toml` and the wiring (`check.py` `done-when-blessed` -> `integrate.py done-when-hold`). The evidence drives all three points and the shared predicate -> ready: the text is closed and traced. Two clauses are still unverified at the TC level: the review-session exemption, and the merge arm naming its digest. That gap belongs to TC-325's return, not to this text\n- [RETURN] TC-325 -> an unblessed in-lane change holds build/rework dispatch and a staged close, with the stated exemptions, and all hold points share one predicate -> its cited test also asserts the merge-ladder refusal, but neither Expected nor Method states the serial-landing hold that SR-156 and LLR-309 require. \"The stated exemptions\" points at no list. The review-session exemption LLR-309 states is asserted by no test -> not ready: the row's own acceptance claim leaves out one of the three hold points it claims to verify, and it leaves one stated exemption unchecked\n- [APPROVE] TC-326 -> only a verdict line or an owner-ruled decision entry binding the current digest releases the holds; an unseen ruling does not; a later different checklist is held again -> the tests drive all three verdict outcomes, an unseen and then a confirmed ruling, and a re-edit after a blessing, at dispatch, staged close and merge -> ready: the obligation is closed and its evidence checks what it says\n- [RETURN] TC-327 -> the done-when and combined classes keep scope, grammar and the shared digest through composition and coordinator routing -> it verifies LLR-308, which goes back to be split and re-parented, so its Verifies and Expected must follow that split. Its Expected (\"retain their scope, grammar and shared digest\") is not one an observer could check, and LLR-308's unreadable-claim and missing-Context refusals, its post-closure claim read and its stated clip are not asserted -> not ready\n- [RETURN] TC-328 -> at merge a changed closed Done-when becomes \"either its covering SUCCESSOR disposition or one scoped done-when adjudication, never both\" -> LLR-262 has three outcomes plus a refusal: an uncovered change mints the done-when row; a CLARITY/BLESSED cover mints NOTHING; a SUCCESSOR cover mints its Done-when part's drafts; an ambiguous or draftless part refuses. The TC's own cited `test_at_merge_a_covered_close_mints_nothing` produces neither of the \"either\" arms -> not ready: the Expected is false for one of its own cases and leaves out the refusal its Method runs. It also duplicates two of TC-257's citations without saying what it adds\n\nApproved: LLR-309, TC-326. Returned: LLR-307, LLR-308, TC-325, TC-327, TC-328. The follow-up work is drafted under `## Dispositions` in `docs/work/active/wi-841/WI-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane.md`.\n\nOUTCOME: RETURN rows=7\n----\n997b4c20 WI-841: Record 