{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfn75xtdNKgsyrDY1hiBu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both amended rows change meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`). I re-anchored neither row: LLR-262 goes back for a rewrite, and LLR-278 can't be re-anchored while LLR-262 is still drifted.\n\n**What changed in each row**\n- **LLR-262 (Detail):** two new cases at the merge-time mint. If the claim can't be read, the mint is refused. If there is no claim, nothing is minted and intake says the check did not run. An intake that was correct under the old text could fail both.\n- **LLR-278 (Detail):** the rule for a WIDENED snapshot now identifies a registry by the file that holds its rows, and covers TOML, legacy CSV and markdown files. An implementation that only matched the TOML path met the old text but fails the new one for CSV or markdown registries.\n\n**What happens next**\n- **LLR-278:** I would bless it.\n- **LLR-262:** I would not bless it as written. The behaviour matches the `kdone.claim_copy` arm in `intake.py`, but the inserted sentence is broken: \"For a readable claim, it whose closed spec's Done-when changed …\" has no verb. \"It\" could mean either the row or the intake. The text also doesn't say whether \"refuses the mint\" fails the whole merge, or where \"states that the check did not run\" is written. I drafted the fix (reword only, behaviour unchanged) under a new `## Dispositions` section in `docs/work/active/wi-841/WI-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane.md`.\n- **Re-anchoring:** I ran `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-278` to confirm it would be refused. It was, naming LLR-262's drifted Detail in `low-level-requirements.toml`, and it wrote nothing. Once LLR-262 is reworded and its meaning-or-clarity question is re-judged, LLR-262 and LLR-278 should be re-attested together in one act.\n\n**Commits (registry cells untouched):**\n- `eaad99ac` — the verdict file `docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/003-ADJUDICATE-264d0e5.md`, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `bd314609` — the Dispositions draft, also with `WI: WI-841`.\n\nThe pre-commit checks passed on both commits.\n\n**For the coordinator:** the spec says the owner ruled on 2026-10-06 that a returned row is fixed inside this lane, not minted as new work. If that applies here, the reword should be done in the lane rather than left for intake to mint at merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":68102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"8f2e847f-272a-4e34-993c-4f6286c4dc4c","timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:42:06.823Z","request_id":"req_011Cfn75xc2Qq83MHZzDdDma"}
